# Nothing this toolkit produces belongs in this checkout. The corpora, the profiles that define
# them, every run's output and the scraped reference material live in the sibling crawlee-lab-data
# repository, and Crawlee's working directory is scratch that goes to a temporary path. See .env.
#
# The entries below are guards, not homes: they catch a run started without a .env, which would
# otherwise drop a corpus back into the tool's tree. They are anchored to the root with a leading
# slash because they name directories the toolkit writes, not names it may not use: unanchored,
# `storage/` also swallowed the package at src/crawlee_lab/storage, so a module added there was
# invisible to git.
/data/
/output/
/profiles/*.yaml
/profiles/*.yml
/storage/
/docs/reference/

# The follow-up this machine actually runs, which holds its own paths and its own prompt. The
# example beside it is the tracked one; what a given machine does with a change is not the tool's.
scripts/on-change.ps1

# Spanish-language tutorial, kept locally
docs/tutorial.md

# Python
__pycache__/
*.py[cod]
*.egg-info/
.venv/
venv/

# Tooling caches
.mypy_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.pytest_cache/
.coverage
htmlcov/

# Environment
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# OS
Thumbs.db
.DS_Store
